{#
  registry's verify Jobs and the ConfigMap that carries their script.

  The renderer emits `templates/verify/*.yaml.j2` into the `registry-verify` Kustomization once
  `registry` reads Ready (D5, Wave D). These Jobs replaced the self-test and netpol probe
  tasks and their three Job templates, which registry's flip deleted.

  THE PULL JOBS RUN A COPY OF THE FLEET'S PYTHON JOB IMAGE FROM THE PUSH STORE (ruling on
  #5680). Their proof is that containerd on each node pulls the pod's own image from
  `{{ k8s_registry_pull_host }}`, and the Job census requires every container to run
  `python3 <mount>/<script>.py`, so the image they pull must hold Python. The push Job writes
  that copy: after its round trip it copies `flux_job_image`'s linux/amd64 image into
  `{{ registry_k8s_probe_repo }}:<seed tag>`, which names the pin's digest. A new pin is a new
  tag, so the pull Jobs rename with it and Flux runs all of them again. Each new pin adds about
  20 MB to the push store, which nothing reclaims on a schedule since its GC was retired.
  monitor-bridge's `pvc_fullness` page at 85% of `registry-data` is the bound (#5752), and
  docs/registry-push-store-gc.md is the operator's collection when it pages.

  DECIDED: the pull Jobs wait for the seed by kubelet's image-pull retry, not by an ordering
  Flux would have to express. Flux applies every Job in `registry-verify` at once, and on a
  first run, or the first after a pin bump, the pull pods start before the push has written
  their image. Such a pod waits in ImagePullBackOff, which is Pending and spends no
  `backoffLimit`. kubelet retries after 10, 20, 40, 80 and 160s, so its sixth attempt lands
  about 310s in. The push's deadline is 240s, so that attempt finds the image whenever the
  push succeeded. The pull deadline, 450s, covers it and the pull itself, and sits below the
  Kustomization's 600s. A failed push leaves the pull Jobs to fail on their deadline as well,
  which names the same fault twice rather than hiding it.

  Both names end in a digest, as the Job census requires (D5, *Rules for every Job Flux
  applies*): the ConfigMap's in `configmap_digest8` of its data, each Job's in
  `job_spec_digest8` of its spec. Each is computed here from the same JSON those functions
  hash, so each spec is written once as YAML text, parsed for the hash and emitted verbatim.
  The renderer passes `flux_job_image` and `flux_job_connect`, the helper's text, to every
  `templates/verify/` file (`render_tag`).

  DECIDED: both specs embed a digest of the rendered NetworkPolicy, Deployment and Service.
  The fence is what the isolation Job tests, and the Deployment and Service are what the push
  Job dials, so an edit to any of them renames both Jobs and makes Flux run them again. The
  Ansible tasks re-run on every deploy; these re-run only when that render changes.

  The caller census (D5, *A fence admits every Job that dials through it*). Every pod runs in
  `k8s_namespace` and execs into nothing:
    - `registry-verify-push-<digest>` carries `app: registry-selftest-push` and dials
      registry:{{ k8s_registry_port }}. `networkpolicy.yaml.j2` already admits that label,
      because the Ansible self-test it replaces carries it, so it needs no new peer. Its seed
      also reads `flux_job_image`'s registry over the WAN, which no fence here covers, because
      egress is not enforced on this cluster (ADR-0009);
    - `registry-verify-pull-<digest>` and, on a cluster with an agent node,
      `registry-verify-pull-agent-<digest>` carry `app: registry-verify` and dial nothing.
      Their image pull is containerd's, which arrives SNAT'd to a node grant the fence already
      holds, so they need no peer either;
    - `registry-verify-isolation-<digest>` carries `app: registry-verify` and dials
      registry:{{ k8s_registry_port }} and registry:{{ k8s_registry_ghcr_mirror_port }}, both
      of which must REFUSE it. No peer is added: admitting `registry-verify` would open the
      hole the Job proves closed. tests/test_registry_verify.py fails if the fence admits it.
#}
{% set script_name = 'registry_verify.py' %}
{% set script_dir = '/verify' %}
{% set data = {
  script_name: lookup('file', playbook_dir + '/roles/k8s/registry/files/' + script_name, rstrip=False),
  'flux_job_connect.py': flux_job_connect,
} %}
{% set configmap_name = 'registry-verify-' + ({'data': data, 'binaryData': {}} | to_json(sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':')) | hash('sha256'))[:8] %}
{% set render_digest8 = ((lookup('template', 'networkpolicy.yaml.j2') + lookup('template', 'deployment.yaml.j2') + lookup('template', 'service.yaml.j2')) | hash('sha256'))[:8] %}
{% set registry_service = 'registry.' + k8s_namespace + '.svc.cluster.local' %}
{% set seed_tag = 'python-' + (flux_job_image.split('@sha256:')[1])[:12] %}
{% set pulled_image = k8s_registry_pull_host + '/' + registry_k8s_probe_repo + ':' + seed_tag %}
{% set pull_env = {'CHECK': 'pull', 'PULLED_IMAGE': pulled_image} %}
{% set checks = [
  {
    'name': 'push',
    'app': 'registry-selftest-push',
    'deadline': 240,
    'env': {
      'CHECK': 'push',
      'REGISTRY_URL': 'http://' + k8s_registry_push_host,
      'REPO': registry_k8s_probe_repo,
      'TAG': 'verify',
      'SOURCE_IMAGE': flux_job_image,
      'PLATFORM': 'linux/amd64',
      'SEED_TAG': seed_tag,
    },
  },
  {
    'name': 'pull',
    'app': 'registry-verify',
    'deadline': 450,
    'image': pulled_image,
    'node': k8s_registry_node,
    'env': pull_env,
  },
  {
    'name': 'isolation',
    'app': 'registry-verify',
    'deadline': 120,
    'env': {
      'CHECK': 'isolation',
      'ISOLATED_URLS': 'http://' + registry_service + ':' + (k8s_registry_port | string) + '/v2/ http://' + registry_service + ':' + (k8s_registry_ghcr_mirror_port | string) + '/v2/',
    },
  },
] %}
{#
  The agent node's pull path: its containerd resolves the mirror to the pinned ClusterIP and
  is admitted by the fence's flannel.1 ipBlock, the grant this leg fails on if that SNAT
  assumption breaks. Rendered only where `k3s_agent_node_ips` names an agent, as
  the deleted Ansible agent half was: a single-node cluster could never schedule it.
#}
{% if k3s_agent_node_ips | default([]) | length > 0 %}
{% set checks = checks + [{
    'name': 'pull-agent',
    'app': 'registry-verify',
    'deadline': 450,
    'image': pulled_image,
    'node': 'daniel-server',
    'env': pull_env,
  }] %}
{% endif %}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: {{ configmap_name }}
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
data:
{% for key, text in data | dictsort %}
  {{ key }}: {{ text | to_json }}
{% endfor %}
{% for check in checks %}
{% set spec_text %}
# A flaky check fails rather than passing on a retry.
backoffLimit: 0
# Below the 600s `manifests_rollout_timeout_default` every `<tag>-verify` Kustomization takes.
activeDeadlineSeconds: {{ check.deadline }}
template:
  metadata:
    labels:
      app: {{ check.app }}
  spec:
    serviceAccountName: registry-verify
    # The Job reads no Kubernetes API, so its pod holds no token.
    automountServiceAccountToken: false
    restartPolicy: Never
    enableServiceLinks: false
{% if check.node is defined %}
    nodeSelector:
      kubernetes.io/hostname: {{ check.node }}
{% endif %}
    securityContext:
      runAsNonRoot: true
      runAsUser: 65534
      runAsGroup: 65534
      seccompProfile:
        type: RuntimeDefault
    containers:
      - name: verify
{% if check.image is defined %}
        image: {{ check.image }}
        # A cached copy would let the pod start with the registry down, the one thing it
        # must not do.
        imagePullPolicy: Always
{% else %}
        image: {{ flux_job_image }}
        imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent
{% endif %}
        command:
          - python3
          - {{ script_dir }}/{{ script_name }}
        env:
{% for key, value in check.env | dictsort %}
          - name: {{ key }}
            value: {{ value | to_json }}
{% endfor %}
          # Renames the Job whenever the fence, Deployment or Service changes; see the note above.
          - name: REGISTRY_RENDER_DIGEST8
            value: "{{ render_digest8 }}"
          - name: PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE
            value: "1"
        resources:
          requests:
            cpu: 10m
            memory: 32Mi
          limits:
            memory: 64Mi
        securityContext:
          allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
          readOnlyRootFilesystem: true
          capabilities:
            drop:
              - ALL
        volumeMounts:
          - name: script
            mountPath: {{ script_dir }}
            readOnly: true
    volumes:
      - name: script
        configMap:
          name: {{ configmap_name }}
{% endset %}
{% set spec = spec_text | from_yaml %}
---
apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: Job
metadata:
  name: registry-verify-{{ check.name }}-{{ (spec | to_json(sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':')) | hash('sha256'))[:8] }}
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
  annotations:
    homelab/job-kind: verify
spec:
{{ spec_text | indent(2, true) }}
{% endfor %}
